course: dictionary
lesson: 9508
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word stew can be a noun, which is a naming word for a thing, or a verb, which is a doing word. The context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Aunty Roisin makes the best stew in Peckham.» Here stew is a meal: a dish of meat or vegetables cooked slowly in liquid in a pot. The clue is that Aunty Roisin makes it, and people make meals.
explain: «He finds a caravan and a man with an iron pot of stew on a fire of sticks.» The pot is on a fire, so stew must be the food cooking in it. Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Stew can be a noun: a meal of meat or vegetables cooked slowly in liquid in a pot, like «beef stew» or «Irish stew».
fact: Stew can be a verb: to cook food slowly in liquid, as in «stewed apples».
fact: The verb forms are stew, stews, stewed and stewing.
fact: Informally, «in a stew» means worried and upset.
fact: Some words look the same but have different jobs, so always check the sentence before you decide what a word means.
exercise: «Jade's mum laughed into her cawl, a Welsh stew.» In this sentence, stew is a | A verb: to cook slowly | A colour | *A noun: a meal | A question word
exercise: «Elodie stays with Aunty Roisin, who makes the best stew in Peckham.» What is the stew here? | A sign on a chair | A worried feeling | *A meal of meat or vegetables cooked slowly in liquid | A fire of sticks
exercise: Which sentence uses stew as a verb, meaning to cook food slowly in liquid? | *They stewed the apples with sugar and water | The pot sat on the fire | Toad got his stew for six shillings | They ate the stew at dinner
test: Dad says, «I'm in a stew about the bills.» What does in a stew mean here? | Very happy | Hungry for dinner | *Worried and upset | Cooking in a big pot
test: What does «stewed apples» tell you about stew? | It is a kind of bread | *It is a verb: the apples were cooked slowly in liquid | It is a noun: a bowl of apples | It is a colour
exam: Stew can be a noun or a verb. Which pair of meanings is correct? | *Noun: a meal cooked slowly in liquid; verb: to cook food slowly in liquid | Noun: a fire; verb: to sleep | Noun: a dog; verb: to bark | Noun: a worry; verb: to eat quickly
